      "problem": "Simplify the expression $|{-3z}|-5\\cdot|4z|.$",
      "worked_solution": "Firstly, since $|{-a}| = |a|,$ we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n|3z|-5\\cdot|4z|.\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3z|-5\\cdot |4z| & = \\\\ |3|\\cdot |z|-5\\cdot |4|\\cdot |z| & = \\\\ 3\\cdot |z|-5\\cdot 4\\cdot |z| & = \\\\ 3\\cdot |z|-20\\cdot |z| & = \\\\ 3|z|-20|z| & = \\\\ -17|z| & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
